8. Declare meaningful prefixes in the query based on the URIs in the yaml
9. Use proper SPARQL syntax to generate valid queries. Your sparql query must produce exactly the results expected by
the text query. Before finalizing each pair, verify: does the SPARQL query contain every constraint stated in the
question, and no constraints absent from the question?
10. If the question does not have one answer/result, you may or may not use LIMIT in SELECT queries (e.g., LIMIT 100) to
avoid too many results. BUT MAKE SURE to REFLECT THIS in the text query!
11. If a term is awkward in the graph, and you are confident it can be rephrased naturally without being inaccurate, do
so
12. The phrasing of the natural language question should be always natural, fluent and not awkward or stilted. Question
should always end with a question mark.

### Final Note:
The ultimate goal is to produce high-quality, diverse, and very meaningful questions together with their corresponding
accurate SPARQL queries that can be executed against the full knowledge graph.

Another essential property is that an expert in the knowledge graph should be able to reproduce the same sparql query
when given text question only.
- You will be rewarded when you generate questions an expert in the domain would ask where the sparql query being
perfectly aligned to the question and accurately answering it.
- You will be penalized if the generated SPARQL query and the text question do not properly align (eg, the sparql query
has constraints unrequested in the question... or misses requested ones)
- You will be also highly penalized if the generated SPARQL query incorrectly answer the text question or provides no
answer when there is one.
- You will be penalized if your question styles are not diverse enough, if questions are of low quality or are phrased
awkwardly.
- Flagging the subgraph as not meaningful when it's hard to generate high quality questions is better than generating
low quality questions.
- Generating fewer high quality questions that a DOMAIN EXPERT may ask is MUCH better than generating more low quality
questions. Quality over quantity.